    "source": "Curated from published Double Metaphone references: (1) words cited in the comments of the original src/double_metaphone.c (caesar, chianti, michael, chemistry, chorus, chore, architect, arch, orchestra, orchid, wachtler, wechsler, tichner, mchugh, mcclellan, czerny, focaccia, bellocchio, bacchus, accident, accede, succeed, bacci, bertucci, edge, edgar, ghislane, ghiradelli, hugh, bough, broughton, laugh, mclaughlin, cough, gough, rough, tough, cagney, tagliaro, biaggi, jose, jacinto, bajador, cabrillo, gallegos, dumb, thumb, rogier, hochmeier, island, isle, carlisle, carlysle, smith, schmidt, snider, schneider, school, schooner, schermerhorn, schenker, resnais, artois, thomas, thames, filipowicz, breaux, zhao, xavier, wasserman, arnow, uomo, womo, ...); (2) the original fuzzy test suite / README data points (mayer, fuzzy, and the empty string); (3) Lawrence Philips' Dr. Dobb's C/C++ Users Journal article (June 2000) example pairs (smith/schmidt/smyth, wasserman/vasserman, arnow/arnoff, uomo/womo, nowak/novak, czerny/zerny); (4) widely mirrored published vector sets of the Apache Commons Codec DoubleMetaphoneTest / Perl Text::DoubleMetaphone family (schulz, schwartz, schweitzer, zachary, katherine, catherine, andrews, powell, jackson, horowitz, witz).",
